Adapted for this project (`acheteur`, 2026-09-21): trimmed to the functions
actually used (Pedersen hash, ECDSA sign/verify, public key derivation),
dropped the `sympy`/`mpmath` dependencies (`is_quad_residue`, `sqrt_mod`,
`pi_as_string` — unused here) in favor of Python's built-in `pow(x, -1, p)`
for modular inverse. Behavior for the retained functions is unchanged from
upstream; see `tests/test_starkex_signature_l7.py` for verification against
StarkWare's own public test vectors.
